Relevant columns & how they can help  

‣ "TIME": numeric epoch‑seconds of the event → filter rows that occurred between 08:00 and 09:00 on 2023‑06‑01 (≈ 1685606400 – 1685610000).  
‣ "SF_CREATED_AT": timestamp of the event → alternative time filter (‘2023‑06‑01 08:00:00’ to ‘2023‑06‑01 09:00:00’).  
‣ "USER_ID": needed to identify / de‑duplicate users.  
‣ "CAMPAIGN_ID" & "CAMPAIGN_API_ID": associate events with a Braze campaign.  
‣ "MESSAGE_VARIATION_ID" & "MESSAGE_VARIATION_API_ID": granular version of the push message.  
‣ "SEND_ID": unique push‑send instance; lets you link send ↔ open ↔ bounce.  
‣ "DISPATCH_ID": another linking key across tables.  
‣ "PLATFORM": iOS, Android, etc. – segment engagement by device type.  
‣ "AD_TRACKING_ENABLED": privacy flag – compare opt‑in vs. opt‑out users.  
‣ "APP_GROUP_ID", "APP_ID": scope the analysis to one mobile app or group if required.  
‣ "COUNTRY", "TIMEZONE", "LANGUAGE", "DEVICE_MODEL", "OS_VERSION", "SDK_VERSION": demographic / device breakdowns.  
‣ Array columns ("STRING_CUSTOM_ATTRIBUTES", …): custom traits which may explain engagement differences.

Typical time conditions you may apply in the WHERE‑clause  
1) Using epoch seconds  
   WHERE "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000  
2) Using timestamps  
   WHERE "SF_CREATED_AT" BETWEEN '2023-06-01 08:00:00' AND '2023-06-01 09:00:00'  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that help you inspect values in the relevant columns.  Replace / adjust the time window if your installation stores timestamps in a different zone.

```sql
--Description: 1) All push‑notification sends that happened in the 08:00–09:00 window on 1‑Jun‑2023 (sample 20 rows)
SELECT "USER_ID",
       "SEND_ID",
       "CAMPAIGN_ID",
       "TIME"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW
WHERE  "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Distinct users who opened a push within the same one‑hour window
SELECT DISTINCT "USER_ID"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW
WHERE  "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Distinct users whose pushes bounced in that hour
SELECT DISTINCT "USER_ID"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_BOUNCE_VIEW
WHERE  "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Sends grouped by campaign to see which campaigns were active (top 20 by volume)
SELECT "CAMPAIGN_ID",
       COUNT(*)             AS "push_notification_sends"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW
WHERE  "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
GROUP  BY "CAMPAIGN_ID"
ORDER  BY "push_notification_sends" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Basic join – sample of sends that were subsequently opened (matching by "SEND_ID")
SELECT s."USER_ID",
       s."SEND_ID",
       s."TIME"            AS "send_time",
       o."TIME"            AS "open_time"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW  s
JOIN   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW  o
      ON s."SEND_ID" = o."SEND_ID"
WHERE  s."TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
AND    o."TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Platforms represented in the send events during that hour
SELECT DISTINCT "PLATFORM"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW
WHERE  "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Countries & languages of users who opened the push
SELECT "COUNTRY",
       "LANGUAGE",
       COUNT(*) AS "opens"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW
WHERE  "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
GROUP  BY "COUNTRY", "LANGUAGE"
ORDER  BY "opens" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Influenced‑open events (user opened the app within influence window) – sample rows
SELECT "USER_ID",
       "SEND_ID",
       "TIME",
       "PLATFORM"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_INFLUENCEDOPEN_VIEW
WHERE  "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Look at custom string attributes on send events (flattened) for the time window
SELECT t."USER_ID",
       f.value::STRING AS "STRING_CUSTOM_ATTRIBUTE"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_SEND_VIEW t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."STRING_CUSTOM_ATTRIBUTES") f
WHERE  t."TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Users with ad‑tracking disabled who still opened a push (privacy‑aware cohort)
SELECT DISTINCT "USER_ID"
FROM   BRAZE_USER_EVENT_DEMO_DATASET.PUBLIC.USERS_MESSAGES_PUSHNOTIFICATION_OPEN_VIEW
WHERE  "AD_TRACKING_ENABLED" = FALSE
AND    "TIME" BETWEEN 1685606400 AND 1685610000
LIMIT  20;
```
